From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0139] sweet-gpu: the statistics line right, and the first whole cleans counted

"The GPU worked N us on each of M" divided N by M although redwood_gpu_worked() already
returns the average (worked_us / worked_n), and "ms in all" divided that average by 1000
instead of multiplying by the count: both numbers were wrong. The single IOLog was also
cut at 256 characters, so the end of it never reached the log, which is what A5 needs to
judge the cache cleaning.

Print the average, the total as average * count / 1000, and split the line in three
(each under 200 characters): (a) submissions, command buffers, buffers named, KB out of
the cache, us per submission and the whole cleans; (b) the GPU time (average, count, the
seven buckets); (c) waits, over, IOSurfaces, buffers and MB.

toMemoryWritten() now counts, when the whole-buffer flag is still clear at entry (a new
surface, or a buffer's first flush), the buffer in gGPUStat.wholeCleans and its size in
gGPUStat.wholeBytes, both zeroed with the rest by bzero(&gGPUStat, ...), and (a) prints
them as "N first cleans of M MB".

Proof in the log, every five seconds in which something was submitted:

  RedwoodGPU: 1204 submissions in 5001 ms: 1500 command buffers and 3400 buffers named, 980 KB out of the cache in 4100 us a submission; 3 first cleans of 24 MB
  RedwoodGPU: the GPU worked 812 us on each of 1204 (0 under 0.1 ms, 2 under 0.25, 40 under 0.5, 1100 under 1, 60 under 2, 2 under 4, 0 longer; 977 ms in all)
  RedwoodGPU: 12 waits of 320 us, 0 over before they began; 60 IOSurfaces taken as buffers in 210 us each; 900 buffers, 120 MB
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
index f6fbd6d..8d9ddeb 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
@@ -194,7 +194,8 @@ static bool gGPUCached;                         /* boot-arg gpu_cached=1 */
 /* What the last seconds' submissions were and cost here, for the log. */
 static struct {
 	uint64_t since, flushing, waiting, taking;      /* times of the processor's clock */
-	uint64_t flushed;                       /* bytes sent out of the cache */
+	uint64_t flushed, wholeBytes;           /* bytes sent out of the cache, and of the first cleans, how big those buffers were */
+	uint32_t wholeCleans;                   /* buffers every page of which was pushed out once (the first time) */
 	uint32_t submissions, commands, buffers, surfaces, waits, over;
 	uint32_t made, given_again;             /* buffers of their own made for programs, and of those kept ones given again */
 	uint64_t making;                        /* ... and the time it took to make the others */
@@ -1166,6 +1167,12 @@ toMemoryWritten(struct gpu_buffer * b)
 	/* a surface is a new buffer every time a program takes it again (each frame): its own flag */
 	bool * whole = b->surface != NULL ? &b->surface->cleanOnce : &b->whole;
 
+	if (!*whole) {
+		/* 0139: the first time, every page is pushed out (see below): how many such buffers and how big */
+		gGPUStat.wholeCleans++;
+		gGPUStat.wholeBytes += b->size;
+	}
+
 	for (uint64_t off = 0; off < b->size; off += PAGE_SIZE) {
 		IOByteCount len = 0;
 		addr64_t pa = b->memory->getPhysicalSegment(off, &len, kIOMemoryMapperNone);
@@ -1343,13 +1350,16 @@ RedwoodGPUUserClient::submit(struct msm_gem_submit * request)
 		absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(gGPUStat.making, &making);
 		IOLog("RedwoodGPU: buffers: %u made in %llu us each, %u kept ones given again (%llu MB kept)\n", gGPUStat.made,
 		    gGPUStat.made ? making / NSEC_PER_USEC / gGPUStat.made : 0, gGPUStat.given_again, fKeptBytes >> 20);
-		IOLog("RedwoodGPU: %u submissions in %llu ms: %u command buffers and %u buffers named, %llu KB out of the cache "
-		    "in %llu us a submission; the GPU worked %llu us on each of %u (%u under 0.1 ms, %u under 0.25, %u under 0.5, "
-		    "%u under 1, %u under 2, %u under 4, %u longer; %llu ms in all); %u waits of %llu us, %u over before they "
-		    "began; %u IOSurfaces taken as buffers in %llu us each; %u buffers, %llu MB\n",
+		IOLog("RedwoodGPU: %u submissions in %llu ms: %u command buffers and %u buffers named, %llu KB out of the "
+		    "cache in %llu us a submission; %u first cleans of %llu MB\n",
 		    gGPUStat.submissions, nanos / NSEC_PER_MSEC, gGPUStat.commands, gGPUStat.buffers,
 		    (gGPUStat.flushed >> 10) / gGPUStat.submissions, flushing / NSEC_PER_USEC / gGPUStat.submissions,
-		    timed ? worked / timed : 0, timed, by[0], by[1], by[2], by[3], by[4], by[5], by[6], worked / 1000,
+		    gGPUStat.wholeCleans, gGPUStat.wholeBytes >> 20);
+		IOLog("RedwoodGPU: the GPU worked %llu us on each of %u (%u under 0.1 ms, %u under 0.25, %u under 0.5, "
+		    "%u under 1, %u under 2, %u under 4, %u longer; %llu ms in all)\n",
+		    worked, timed, by[0], by[1], by[2], by[3], by[4], by[5], by[6], worked * timed / 1000);
+		IOLog("RedwoodGPU: %u waits of %llu us, %u over before they began; %u IOSurfaces taken as buffers in "
+		    "%llu us each; %u buffers, %llu MB\n",
 		    gGPUStat.waits, gGPUStat.waits ? waiting / NSEC_PER_USEC / gGPUStat.waits : 0, gGPUStat.over,
 		    gGPUStat.surfaces, gGPUStat.surfaces ? taking / NSEC_PER_USEC / gGPUStat.surfaces : 0, fBufferCount,
 		    fBufferBytes >> 20);
